    "summary": "Epic Truckin' > Dark Star > Comes A Time and tight jams throughout",
    "blurb": "The show features an explosive Truckin' → Dark Star → Comes A Time sequence, plus soaring Bird Song and a powerful closing Not Fade Away > Goin' Down > Not Fade Away peel. Jerry's guitar is space‑y and commanding while the rhythm section locks in tight throughout. Soundboard recordings capture the performance with excellent clarity.",
    "review": "July 18, 1972 at Roosevelt Stadium captures the Dead in top form, rolling through a three‑set marathon that still feels fresh today. The second set’s centerpiece – Truckin' into Dark Star and then into Comes A Time – is nothing short of transcendent; Garcia’s tone soars, Keith Godchaux adds shimmering piano textures, and Bill Kreutzmann drives the groove with relentless energy. The first set offers bright moments like Bird Song and a crisp Bertha, while the third set closes with an unforgettable Not Fade Away → Goin' Down The Road Feeling Bad → Not Fade Away triple‑peel that leaves the crowd buzzing. Across all recordings the band is locked in, delivering tight transitions, inspired solos, and vocal harmonies that highlight Bob Weir’s and Jerry’s singing alike. For anyone seeking a quintessential early‑’70s experience, this night stands out as one of the era’s most rewarding performances.",
